From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:17:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/79] dsv41: engine-native compute lane (opt-in
 TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE)

A request that lists {"type": "code_interpreter"}, or offers the lane's own
python function definition, gets a built-in python tool. Its reply holds at
each EOS (Request.hold_eos): the stream keeps its slot and KV, and the
engine skips it while the server runs the calls in the sandboxed executor.
The server renders the template's tool-result turn and resumes the stream
with those tokens as forced rows, so the model continues with the same ids
a client round trip would send, without re-prefilling.

- lanes: hold_eos/held on Stream, a held EOS stays pending (window cut),
  hold.resumeHeld and hold.runnableCount for the idle checks
- lane host: resume_held queued like cancel and applied on the engine
  thread; at most one resume a hold; a held request never goes lone
- engine API: Request.hold_eos, Info.compute, vtable resume_held and
  engine_hold.zig (the executor, Resume, resumeHeld)
- server: compute_turns (opt-in, arming, client stream filter; DeepSeek's
  native tool check for the client's own tools) and compute_segments
  (segment loop, result insertion, merged reply with tensorfold.compute);
  Generation.readText is the reply reading finish and the segment loop
  share; deadline_s carries across segments
- serve: __compute_sandbox trampoline entry in main (Linux)
- dsv41: TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE and its _WORKERS, _MAX_MS, _MAX_RESULT_TOKENS,
  _MAX_CALLS, _MEM_MB, _PYTHON and _CPUS knobs on the CUDA serve path

Not armed: stop strings, structured output, a forced call, logprobs,
background or zero-token requests, and Kimi's native reply reader.
Flag unset: no pool, hold_eos never set, replies unchanged.

test-compute-hold-host (lanes and lane host), test-compute-lane-http-host
(a held python call's result forced in as the template's tool turn through
the chat route, the filter, the definition) and test-lane-api-host.
